# Variables and conditions
@scenario tutorial_lesson_07
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger guide thoughtful]
ginger: Have we met before? A flag lets me remember a yes or a no the next time you visit.
[flag example_ready]
[if example_ready]
ginger: This line appears because the flag is true.
[endif]
ginger: Change the condition to its opposite and replay the example.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
ginger: What keeps a flag value between dialogue lines?
> A story variable. -> correct
> A label name. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: The flag writes state and the condition reads it. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: The flag writes state and the condition reads it.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_07]
[flag tutorial_done_07]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_1]
